                <pb facs="0081" n="69" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg69"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">883.6363/93: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Egypt</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-02-29T17:00:00-04:00">February 29,
                            1944—5 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>413. Your 232 of February 2, 1944 and 306 of February 10, 1944. Please keep the
                    Department fully informed with respect to the reasons for the new 15 percent
                    export duty, the nature of the application envisaged and particularly the
                    effects it may have upon the development of American petroleum interests in
                    Egypt.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
